#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186111840 :tutorial/content "When solving problems with angles, it is helpful to remember the following classifications:\n\n- a **null** angle has a measure of $0^\\circ,$\n\n- an **acute** angle has a measure between $0^\\circ$ and $90^\\circ,$\n\n- a **right** angle has a measure of $90^\\circ,$\n\n- an **obtuse** angle has a measure between $90^\\circ$ and $180^\\circ,$\n\n- a **straight** angle has a measure of $180^\\circ,$\n\n- a **reflex** angle has a measure between $180^\\circ$ and $360^\\circ,$ and\n\n- a **full** angle has a measure of $360^\\circ.$\n\nIt is also helpful to remember that when two lines meet at a point, the opposite angles are called **vertical angles**. Vertical angles are congruent, and consequently they have the same measure." :tutorial/id #uuid "282e8601-d3f4-5c34-a96b-a071a96de244" :tutorial/math-academy-id 2182 :tutorial/title "Introduction"}]}
